silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_13_regression_test_suite_sections_05_probe_ungated_render_concrete_anchor_7#geometricgapforungatedshortcut silm:hasLongDescription "The GeometricGapForUngatedShortcut is The blank cells in the lower row of the R5 tikzcd between SourcePhrase_lower and the trailing empty columns are intentional layout: they record the geometric distance that the dashed-red ungated arrow must cross. The visible reach of the forbidden shortcut from the lower row up to RenderedDiagram is what makes the negative-regression case readable. Were the cells filled, the shortcut would be a short side-arrow and would lose its rhetorical force as the rule-breaking long jump from raw source to proof surface. For the Mittens fixture, this is the visual representation that \"Mittens measured at 4.1kg on 2024-11-01\" -> rendered figure SKIPS ingest, type, AND validate — three named gates, three blank cells." .
